<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tibor Szamuely</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1890–1919</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tibor Szamuely was a Hungarian communist leader of the Hungarian Soviet Republic of 1919, in which he served as a deputy people's commissar for military affairs. He organised the repression of counter-revolutionary uprisings and was associated with the terror squad known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lenin-boys">Lenin Boys</a>. After the regime's collapse he died while trying to flee across the Austrian border in August 1919.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tibor-szamuely.jpg" alt="Tibor Szamuely" width="320" height="455" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tiborslibor.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
